---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Patio Tile Layout Planner — Cuts, Pieces & Boxes" description="Visualize a rectangular patio tile layout. Compare centered and corner starts, see edge cuts, and estimate tile pieces and boxes from your own measurements.">
<header class="container page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Measure. Compare. Make a plan.</p><h1>A clearer picture<br/>of your <em>tile layout.</em></h1><p class="lead">See full tiles and edge cuts before buying. Compare two straight-grid layouts with your actual tile dimensions.</p></header>
<section class="container tile-workspace">
<form id="tile-form" class="tile-form" novalidate>
<fieldset><legend><span>1</span> Your measured floor</legend><p class="small">Rectangular floors only. Enter feet and remaining inches, not the size printed on a floor plan.</p><div class="tile-field-pair"><div><label for="floor-width-feet">Floor width · feet</label><input id="floor-width-feet" inputmode="decimal" type="text" value="10"/></div><div><label for="floor-width-inches">Additional inches</label><input id="floor-width-inches" inputmode="decimal" type="text" value="0"/></div><div><label for="floor-depth-feet">Floor depth · feet</label><input id="floor-depth-feet" inputmode="decimal" type="text" value="8"/></div><div><label for="floor-depth-inches">Additional inches</label><input id="floor-depth-inches" inputmode="decimal" type="text" value="0"/></div></div><button type="button" id="tile-swap" class="reset-button">Swap floor width &amp; depth</button></fieldset>
<fieldset><legend><span>2</span> Your tile &amp; gaps</legend><div class="tile-field-pair"><div><label for="tile-width">Actual tile width (in)</label><input id="tile-width" inputmode="decimal" type="text" value="12"/></div><div><label for="tile-depth">Actual tile length (in)</label><input id="tile-depth" inputmode="decimal" type="text" value="24"/></div><div><label for="tile-joint">Joint between tiles (in)</label><input id="tile-joint" inputmode="decimal" type="text" value="0.125"/></div><div><label for="tile-perimeter">Perimeter gap, each edge (in)</label><input id="tile-perimeter" inputmode="decimal" type="text" value="0.25"/></div></div><p class="small">Example numbers, not installation recommendations. Use the exact tile/system requirements for joint and perimeter gaps. A decimal point or comma works; enter up to four decimal places. Zero gaps are a geometry option only.</p></fieldset>
<fieldset><legend><span>3</span> Layout &amp; shopping allowance</legend><label for="tile-layout">Start the grid</label><select id="tile-layout"><option value="centered">Centered · balance opposite edge cuts</option><option value="corner">Corner · full tile at upper-left</option></select><label for="tile-rotation">Tile direction</label><select id="tile-rotation"><option value="0">Width runs across the floor</option><option value="90">Turn tiles 90°</option></select><div class="tile-field-pair"><div><label for="tile-extra">Extra pieces (%)</label><input id="tile-extra" inputmode="decimal" type="text" value="10"/></div><div><label for="tile-per-box">Pieces per box (optional)</label><input id="tile-per-box" inputmode="numeric" type="text" value=""/></div></div><label for="tile-box-price">Price per box in USD (optional)</label><input id="tile-box-price" inputmode="decimal" type="text" value=""/><p class="small">Extras are your choice. No offcut reuse is assumed: each drawn tile position needs one new source tile. Box rounding is shown separately.</p></fieldset>
<div class="plan-actions"><button class="button" type="submit">Update tile plan →</button><button class="reset-button" type="reset">Reset example</button></div><p class="small">Updates as you type when measurements are valid. Calculations stay in your browser. Up to 2,500 drawn pieces; no account required.</p><noscript><p>JavaScript is needed for the drawing and calculations. The planning guide below is available without it.</p></noscript>
</form>
<section id="tile-results" class="tile-results" aria-labelledby="tile-result-heading"><header class="tile-print-brand"><img src="/assets/wordmark.svg" alt="Little Home Ideas" width="420" height="70"/><p>Small ideas. Better living. · littlehomeideas.com</p></header><p class="eyebrow">A layout, not an installation specification</p><h2 id="tile-result-heading">Your floor, piece by piece.</h2><p id="tile-status" class="small" role="status"></p><p id="tile-error" class="form-error" role="alert" hidden></p><div id="tile-summary" class="tile-metrics"></div><div id="tile-canvas"></div><p class="tile-legend"><span class="legend-full">Full tile</span><span class="legend-cut">Cut position</span><span>Light background = joints / perimeter gap</span></p><p id="tile-selected" class="small" aria-live="polite"></p><p class="small tile-keyboard">Select a tile to see its dimensions. Tab into the drawing, then use arrow keys to choose a piece.</p><div id="tile-layout-comparison"></div><div id="tile-estimate"></div><details id="tile-cuts"><summary>Cut sizes &amp; quantities</summary><div id="tile-cut-list"></div></details><div class="plan-actions tile-export"><button class="button" type="button" id="tile-download">Download plan</button><button class="button secondary" type="button" id="tile-image">Download drawing (SVG)</button><button class="button secondary" type="button" id="tile-print">Print plan</button></div><p class="small tile-warning">Rectangular floor, straight grid, cuttable tiles. No obstacles, drainage design, movement-joint layout, adhesive/grout quantities, structural approval, or offcut nesting. Do not use this count for interlocking deck tiles or pedestal systems without checking their rules.</p><footer class="tile-print-url">littlehomeideas.com/tools/patio-tile-planner/</footer></section>
</section>
<section class="container tile-guide prose"><h2>Read the plan before you shop</h2><h3>Why dividing floor area by tile area is not enough</h3><p>Edge cuts consume source tiles too. In a 3 × 7 ft rectangle with 14.4 × 14.4 in tiles and zero gaps, a corner grid has 18 positions: 10 full tiles and 8 cut positions. The floor area alone suggests 15 tiles after rounding. This planner allows one source tile for each of the 18 positions; it does not assume you can reuse the offcuts.</p><h3>Compare the edges</h3><p>Centered mode compares a central tile with a central joint on each axis, then uses the alignment with wider, balanced edge pieces. Corner mode starts with a full tile at the upper-left. A layout with fewer positions may have less attractive cuts. Look at the drawing and grouped cut list before choosing.</p><h3>Keep extras and box rounding separate</h3><p>For a base allowance of 18 pieces, choosing 10% extra adds 2 pieces, for 20 required. With 8 pieces per box, that becomes 3 boxes and 24 purchased pieces. The 4 additional pieces come from box rounding; they are separate from the 2 requested extras. Prices are calculated only from the box price you enter.</p><h3>Check the real installation</h3><p>Use actual tile dimensions and dry-layout a sample where appropriate. A uniform grid cannot account for an out-of-square floor or an obstacle. Schluter's <a href="https://www.schluter.com/schluter-us/en_US/faq/ditra-ditraxl-movement-joints-tile-installation" rel="noopener noreferrer">movement-joint guidance</a> explains that uncoupling does not eliminate movement joints. The <a href="https://www.ceramictilefoundation.org/homeowners-guide-to-hiring-qualified-tile-installer" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ceramic Tile Education Foundation's homeowner guide</a> covers installer qualifications and installation planning. A perimeter-gap input here does not design the required movement joints.</p><p>For an outdoor floor or elevated balcony, have the proposed system checked for suitability, waterproofing, drainage, thresholds, and permitted loads. Follow the exact manufacturer's instructions and obtain professional/building guidance where needed. This tool supplies geometry and arithmetic, not installation approval.</p><p>Still arranging the space? Open the <a href="/tools/patio-privacy-planner/">Patio &amp; Balcony Layout Planner</a> to place furniture, plants, walls, and screening. Our <a href="/articles/small-patio-furniture-layout/">small-patio furniture guide</a> helps you collect the measurements first.</p></section>
<script type="module" src="/assets/tile-planner.js?v=tiles-20261015" is:inline></script>
</Base>
